From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Janne Grunau <j@jannau.net>
Date: Fri, 26 Sep 2025 09:37:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] power: reset: macsmc-reboot: Prevent probing without of_node

MFD will probe sub devices declared with MFD_CELL_OF() even without
match on the device tree compatible. macsmc-reboot depends on nvmem
provided via device tree. Fail probe() with -ENODEV if this information
is missing.

Signed-off-by: Janne Grunau <j@jannau.net>
(cherry picked from commit 34acdd7dbd8538bc66bafce6cbe8d6563cf391e2)
---
 drivers/power/reset/macsmc-reboot.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/reset/macsmc-reboot.c b/drivers/power/reset/macsmc-reboot.c
index 9fc36fa..7688cfd 100644
--- a/drivers/power/reset/macsmc-reboot.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/macsmc-reboot.c
@@ -204,6 +204,14 @@ static int macsmc_reboot_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct macsmc_reboot *reboot;
 	int ret, i;
 
+	/*
+	 * MFD will probe this device even without a node in the device tree,
+	 * thus bail out early if the SMC on the current machines does not
+	 * support reboot and has no node in the device tree.
+	 */
+	if (!pdev->dev.of_node)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
 	reboot = devm_kzalloc(&pdev->dev, sizeof(*reboot), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!reboot)
 		return -ENOMEM;
